# <%= current_page.data.title %>

AWS Transform custom can be used from your local machine with the AWS Transform CLI. This guide covers the platform-specific setup needed by Modernisation Platform users. For the full AWS Transform custom guide, see the [AWS Transform CLI getting started documentation](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/transform/latest/userguide/custom-get-started.html).

## Access and permissions

The AWS Transform CLI uses AWS credentials to authenticate. You do not need to use the AWS Transform web application or AWS IAM Identity Center to use the CLI.

The required AWS Transform permissions have been added to the Modernisation Platform developer role. Use temporary credentials for that role, as described in [Getting AWS Credentials](getting-aws-credentials.html), and select the account and region where you want to run the transformation.

## Note regarding Regions

The [getting started guide](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/transform/latest/userguide/custom-get-started.html\#custom-region-configuration) shows the regions where Transform us supported.

As of writing and following the experiences of users, we recommend setting the default region to eu-central-1 (Frankfurt) as using eu-west-2 has been known to result in errors.

## Prerequisites

You need:

- Node.js 22 or later
- Git
- a working directory that is a Git repository
- an internet connection that can reach the endpoints listed in the [AWS Transform network requirements](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/transform/latest/userguide/custom-get-started.html#custom-network-requirements)

Install the AWS CLI if it is not already available on your machine. Follow AWS's [AWS CLI installation instructions](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cli/latest/userguide/getting-started-install.html), then configure credentials using [Getting AWS Credentials](getting-aws-credentials.html).

## Install the AWS Transform CLI

Follow AWS's [AWS Transform CLI installation instructions](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/transform/latest/userguide/custom-get-started.html#custom-installation).

On macOS, run:

```shell
curl -fsSL https://transform-cli.awsstatic.com/install.sh | bash
```

Check that the installation succeeded:

```shell
atx --version
```

## Configure authentication and region

Configure the AWS credentials for the Modernisation Platform developer role using the [AWS credentials instructions](getting-aws-credentials.html). The CLI supports the same AWS profiles and environment variables as the AWS CLI.

Set the region to London, which is the AWS Transform region used by the Modernisation Platform:

```shell
export AWS_REGION=eu-west-2
```

If you use an AWS CLI profile, set it for the current shell instead:

```shell
export AWS_PROFILE=<your-profile-name>
```

## Run a transformation

Change to a Git repository containing the code you want to transform and start the CLI:

```shell
atx
```

You can then ask the agent to run a transformation, for example:

```text
Execute the AWS/java-aws-sdk-v1-to-v2 transformation on the codebase at ./my-java-project
```

For non-interactive execution and the available command options, see the [AWS Transform CLI command reference](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/transform/latest/userguide/custom-command-reference.html).

Review the changes made by the transformation with standard Git commands, such as `git status`, `git diff`, and `git log`.

